1.4.1 Aug 11, 2026
====================

* Pass secrets to dump.sh via the environment instead of command line arguments
* Pass the configured `tunnel` through to dump.sh during backup, where it was
  previously dropped. Tunneling still does not work with the published image:
  `dump.sh` shells out to `ssh`, and `openssh-client` is not installed. Using a
  tunnel requires a derived image that adds it.
* Pin GitHub Actions to commit SHAs
* Add integration test suite, running in CI on every pull request

1.4.0 Jul 24, 2025
====================

* Add support for generic custom labels in monitor configuration
* Improve documentation for monitor configuration with usage examples

1.3.2 Jan 30, 2024
====================

* Fix `/app` requiring write permissions for the unprivileged user

1.3.1 Jan 30, 2024
====================

* Fix user home directory requiring write permissions

1.3.0 Jan 29, 2024
====================

* Run the container as a dedicated unprivileged `dumptruck` user (uid 2000)
  instead of root

1.2.4 Aug 10, 2023
====================

* Re-tag of 1.2.3, no changes

1.2.3 Aug 10, 2023
====================

* Fix cleanup deleting backups whose name merely starts with the configured
  prefix

1.2.2 Mar 23, 2023
====================

* Build multi-platform images (linux/amd64, linux/arm64)
* Rename the release workflow to `build.yml` and add a build status badge

1.2.1 Mar 22, 2023
====================

* Fix image name in the container build

1.2.0 Mar 22, 2023
====================

First tagged release since 1.0, containing everything below plus:

* Add RavenDB as a supported database type
  - back up multiple databases, and existing collections only
  - restore a single database selected by regex, creating it if needed
  - allow self-signed certificates
  - clean up local RavenDB backups
* Add a backup status metric and source labels for monitoring
* Add restore functionality
* Support rclone for storing dumps
* Print the backup path
* Use PostgreSQL 10 from the upstream repo
* Fix cleanup adding a dot to the prefix
* Update encryption method
* Publish container builds to ghcr.io instead of Docker Hub, via an automated
  release workflow

1.2 Dec 20, 2018
====================

* Use official mongo 3.6 tools instead of debian package
* Fix mongorestore to a different database
* Improve logging for backup operations and errors
* add `SSH_TUNNEL_KEY` environment variable for configuring the SSH tunnel key

1.1 Dec 20, 2018
====================

* Add a command to backup a single source only
* Remove multi-buildpack build, now supporting docker only
  - multi-buildpack was slow to `cf push` iterate
  - multi-buildpack also had problems with postgresql clients
* Enhance docker auto-configuration to consumer `*_CONFIG_JSON` environment variables
  - now writes `*_CONFIG_JSON` env vars to individual `*.config.json` files

1.0 Oct 17, 2018
====================

* Initial release
